{"study_accession":"PRJEB111352","secondary_study_accession":"ERP191966","title":"Polysome associated transcriptome in nonactivated and activated human CD8+ T cells","description":"To capture the rapid changes of gene expression and translation upon T cell activation, we measured the transcriptome of total cell lysates and matched polysomal fractionation from non-activated primary human CD8+ effector T cells, and from CD8+ T cells that were reactivated for 2h with PMA-ionomycin. For polysome fractionation, we isolated RNA from 15 sucrose fractions (17-50% sucrose gradient), which based on 18S/28S ribosomal subunit distribution we pooled into ribosome-free, monosome-bound, polysome light and polysome heavy-bound RNA. Fractions were then purified and concentrated with RNA Clean & Concentrator-5 kit (Zymo Research). RNA for the whole cell transcriptome analysis was isolated with Quick-RNA Microprep kit (Zymo Research). RNA-sequencing analysis RNA-sequencing reads were quasi-mapped on the human transcriptome GRCh38 from Gencode (version 38, October 2021) using Salmon tool version 1.5.2. An average of 33×1e6 reads for each sample was mapped to the transcriptome. ","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":30,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMEA122125736","study_accession":"PRJEB111352","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"donor pool 1 nonactivated full","description":"Human CD8+ T cell","sex":"","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-04-26","attributes":[["ENA-CHECKLIST","ERC000011:1.3"],["organism","Homo sapiens"],["collection date","2019-09-14"],["scientific_name","Homo sapiens"],["common name","human"],["geographic location (country and/or sea)","Netherlands"],["isolation_source","human blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"ERR16987344","experiment_accession":"ERX16370992","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"Inverse rRNA selection","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":156861402,"base_c